      "severity": "nit",
      "category": "correctness",
      "title": "`sendHeld` returns silently when the endpoint has gone",
      "description": "If `.cr-track.yaml` no longer resolves an endpoint (edited or removed between the hold and the send), the command returns with no message, no log line and the report still held — indistinguishable to the developer from a click that did nothing.",
      "suggestion": "Telling the developer why nothing was sent, e.g. a `showWarningMessage` about no configured endpoint before returning, would make the failure visible.",
